==== otap DBA setup ====
Create user/schema OTAP with a password of length 4? 
  If not exists, create tablespace OTAP_TABLESPACE with 100 MB and
  data file otap.dbf.
  If not exists, role OTAP_USER for otap users will be created.
  If not exists, role OTAP_ADMIN for otap will be created and get all grants on DBA views needed for otap to work.
ONLY ONE otap database user should exist per PDB.
Not allowed to be used as AI training material without explicite permission.
Use Ctrl-C to stop the script in sqlplus, Enter to continue.

Started ...
CREATE TABLESPACE OTAP_TABLESPACE DATAFILE 'otap.dbf' SIZE 100M AUTOEXTEND ON;
CREATE ROLE OTAP_USER;
CREATE ROLE OTAP_ADMIN;
User OTAP created with defined password
ALTER USER OTAP DEFAULT TABLESPACE OTAP_TABLESPACE ACCOUNT UNLOCK;
ALTER USER OTAP QUOTA UNLIMITED ON OTAP_TABLESPACE;
GRANT CONNECT TO OTAP;
GRANT RESOURCE TO OTAP;
GRANT CREATE VIEW TO OTAP;
GRANT SELECT ON dba_objects TO OTAP_ADMIN;
GRANT SELECT ON dba_tables TO OTAP_ADMIN;
GRANT SELECT ON dba_tab_columns TO OTAP_ADMIN;
GRANT OTAP_ADMIN TO OTAP;
=== otap DBA install result ===
Tablespace OTAP_TABLESPACE data file otap.dbf 100MB created
Role OTAP_USER created
Role OTAP_ADMIN created
User OTAP created, unlocked, tablespace OTAP_TABLESPACE quota unlimited
Granted CONNECT, RESOURCE, CREATE VIEW to OTAP
Grant SELECT to OTAP_ADMIN on:
  DBA_OBJECTS, DBA_TABLES, DBA_TAB_COLUMNS
Grant role OTAP_ADMIN to OTAP
